can apple's new studio display keep up  with the much more expensive pro display  xdr  well in many ways yeah  actually it can and there are five  specific ways that it is actually better  we've been testing and using the 5k  studio display for a week now and i've  personally owned the 6k pro display xdr  for over two years so in this video i'll  be comparing everything from display  quality flexibility features performance  and much more after many years of people  complaining apple finally made another  display but it cost five thousand  dollars and that was without a way to  mount it which costs at least 200 more  if you just buy the vasa adapter or a  shocking one thousand dollars for the  stand and the pro stand 9.99 and like  the mac pro they'll all be available in  this in the fall thankfully two years  later we have something that is still  expensive but way more attainable  especially for those of you guys that  make a living with your mac coming in at  1600 instead of 6 000 now this is for  the version that doesn't have height  adjustability whereas the xdr stand can  be adjusted and raised much higher but  for 400 bucks more you can get the  height adjustable model personally i  would rather get a little base if you  need a few inches higher because the  distance from the wall will change while  you are adjusting it because of that arm  so if you have a small desk it could end  up feeling a little bit too close to you  now with that said i ended up getting  used to it sitting slightly too low for  my taste after a few days of use and  that's without having any neck or strain  issues or anything like that  so we are just going to leave it the way  it is now the xcrs luxury stand attaches  with ultra strong magnets and can also  be set vertically which is something  that you cannot do with the studio  display even if you buy the more  expensive stand the only way to do this  is to get the vasa option that  thankfully doesn't cost anymore and then  get your own third-party stand now as  far as the build quality both are  excellent being built fully out of  aluminum and glass this is why so many  people have been asking apple to build  another display because most monitors on  the market are made out of cheap plastic  with a plastic film on the front which  has lower contrast and more reflectivity  than the glass with these displays with  that they not only look good but these  monitors are super stable on your desk  compared to the previous 5k the apple  sold from lg now if you've used higher  end monitors before that can get really  bright you will know that some of them  actually have fans that you can hear now  both of these have dual fans but they  are silent the studio display sucks and  air from the vents on the bottom that  cover the full length and then exhaust  them from the top the xdr on the other  hand has that iconic cheese grater  pattern on the back that helps cool it  down and the crazy thing is that the  pattern is the reason for most of the  thickness of the 6a xdr so with that why  in the world is a studio display so  thick when it doesn't have those well  there are two reasons the first one is  that this display has a literal iphone  11 processor in it with an a13 chip  that's paired with 64 gigabytes of fast  storage and four gigs of ram now i'm  going to touch on this in just a bit but  the second reason is because apple may  use this frame for an upcoming imac  which is also possibly why it has so  many vent holes on the bottom and the  top even though it does not need that  because it doesn't have mini led now for  some reason apple decided to use a  mostly non-removable power cable linus  tech tips did yank it out with a lot of  effort so you can actually remove it but  apple designed a tool specifically for  removing this which is just dumb why not  just use a normal plug like the 6k pro  display xdr has now both these connect  through thunderbolt with three extra usb  type-c ports to use as a hub now this is  where the studio display is very  impressive somehow apple is able to get  around the previous five gigabit per  second bandwidth limitation since the 5k  display uses so much data now possibly  because of the a13 doing processing i'm  not sure i have no idea but what i do  know is that technically the ports are  twice as fast than the 6k pro display  xdr and in the real world i noticed the  same exact difference when i'm testing  with an external fast ssd now with that  said the 6k actually only runs at usb  type 2 speeds when connected to my mac  pro's vega 2 graphics card because of  different limitations and you don't have  that issue with the studio display and  the benefits of the studio don't stop  there with the xdr i had to spend over  200 on speakers well i guess i didn't  have to spend 200 bucks on those but i  also didn't want some junk speakers if i  spent so much on the display so you're  gonna buy something decent that sounds  good  whereas the suit display has six  speakers built into it four of them are  force canceling woofers that actually  have really nice deep bass surprisingly  deep as well as two speakers for the  higher frequencies just like the new  16-inch macro pros the sound quality is  very very good take a listen for  yourself  [Music]  now i have to say it doesn't get as loud  as an imac but it does sound more  natural and with deeper bass and so for  most regular people these speakers are  more than good enough for daily use and  they also support spatial audio with  dolby atmos support and with hey siri  using the built-in mics here's the  quality of the 1080p webcam that's built  into the studio display as well as the  triple microphones now this actual  webcam is really wide it's center stage  same one that's built into the ipads  which means that right now when i'm  recording with the application that  doesn't support it you it actually just  crops in a lot to look like a normal one  but you guys could see the quality is  not great we have some noise not as good  detail but it does allow you to use the  center stage feature to go much further  away it will auto adjust and then if  somebody else walks into the frame  well you will see them actually show  vadim just like it showed right now so  it is nice to have it built in but i do  wish the quality was a little bit better  the 6k xdr doesn't have a webcam or  microphones built in so you once again  need to spend more and then you could  choose between something junky or  something good like logitech's 4k pro  webcam that can magnetically attach to  the xdr which does look fairly clean but  of course that is another add-on i have  to say that it is nice to have  everything you need built into the  display to have a nice clean setup to  not to spend extra money but with that  said well let's get into what makes the  xdr worth that 6 000 price tag the image  quality now yes 6k does sound like a lot  more than 5k it has just over 20 million  pixels whereas the 5k studio has just  under 15 million so in the real world it  is nowhere as big of a difference when  you're comparing say 4k to 5k and with  that since the pro display is larger at  32 inches you are actually not getting  any extra detail those extra pixels are  needed to keep the same 218 pixels per  inch which apple considers retina  quality so the actual sharpness and  detail on these are identical both of  these look really really good really  detailed at normal viewing distances  unlike a 4k display which looks a lot  worse at this size and distance now the  xdr's biggest selling point is that it  can sustain a massive 1 000 it's a  brightness across the entire display all  at once with no limitations and up to  1600 nits in certain scenarios and  depending on what's being shown this is  crazy because most 4k displays even the  best oled ones  they actually max out at less than a  thousand that's only for certain little  specks of  highlights on the screen if you have a  full screen brightness it'll be at like  300. and if you're comparing that to  most budget 4k displays that people say  you just buy that while you spend so  much money well those are running at  about 300 nits nowhere near that now  apple's new studio display disappointed  many people because it is not mini led  so it cannot hit those crazy high  brightness levels many people said that  it has the same panel as the 5k imax and  lg's six-year-old ultrafine 5k display  that has the same panel as the imax and  that is why so many people were so  bummed out and disappointed but that is  simply not true the studio display is a  hundred nits brighter at 600 nits which  is extremely bright for an sdr monitor  but at the same time it actually manages  to have better contrast and way less  reflectivity as well this is clearly a  new updated panel that looks a lot  better and it can also support apple's  edr for really good hdr performance  being a regular lcd panel so the studio  display actually does a surprisingly  good job compared to other displays but  of course the pro display xdr absolutely  kills it with its high brightness for  hdr content with highlights that really  stand out they just pop so much and then  having the full screen brightness that  can literally blind you in dark  environments and with that if you are  watching in the dark you will notice  that the studio display will look great  now not as bad as the imax and other  displays but nothing like the oled  levels of blacks with the pro display  xdr however if you're watching in normal  lighting environments the blacks on the  studio display look surprisingly good  for an lcd display now when you're not  viewing or working with hdr content the  pro display xdr will max out at 500 nits  just like all of the other macs but the  studio display is brighter at 600 which  i really appreciate as it can help  battle reflections and it is really nice  and bright rooms both of these can be  purchased with nano texture to decrease  reflections with way less of a detail  hit compared to matte displays but this  option costs a thousand dollars on the  prospect xdr where it is only 300 on the  studio display with that said most  people do not need this and without it  you will get the full quality of the  display and with the extra brightness of  the studio display it comes out on top  as far as color accuracy both of these  come with dci p3 color accuracy and are  factory calibrated and they have  reference modes depending on the color  space you want to work in but the xdr  has that hdr mode built in and both  these are 10 bit displays with over 1  billion colors if you're somebody that  needs to accurately edit hdr content  then you need the pro display 6k or some  other third-party option that can  support higher brightness but for most  people the studio display simply makes  way more sense it is way better in most  ways and you have all the conveniences  of the built in the speakers you know  the microphone the webcam and all of  that for a much lower price i know the  studio display has gotten a lot of hate  because it is still sdr and because it's  not cheap but prices on everything have  gone up a lot in the last six years  since the lg 5k was released and this  one cost 300 more you're getting a lot  more than three hundred dollars of value  compared to buying that still for  thirteen hundred a lot more built-in  better build quality better resale so i  would say that if you can afford it i do  not think that you will be disappointed  pick one up we'll have a link down below  you will be happy now if you can afford  the 6k version i would still say  pick the 5k version up don't buy that  one unless you need hdr and if you want  to spend that much money i would see if  you can hold off a little bit longer for  apple to update it with some newer specs  and newer features so there you guys go  there's a full comparison i do think  that the studio display is the better  display in most ways but let me know  your thoughts down below click that  circle above if you want to help us  reach our goal of 1 million subscribers  we would definitely appreciate it and  check out one of those great videos  right over there this has been max with  max tech and i will see you in the next  video  [Music]

